cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "MedTrajectory: multi-type longitudinal health-event trajectory modelling"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of MedTrajectory, a decoder-only autoregressive model
  over multi-type clinical event sequences with absolute age and continuous
  relative-time (RoPE) representations, together with the trajectory-generation
  and fixed-horizon risk evaluation protocols, the Track R / Track G contracts,
  and the MIMIC-IV cross-setting replication pipeline.
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-16"
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yang-shuai-yu/MedTrajectory"
url: "https://github.com/yang-shuai-yu/MedTrajectory"
type: software
keywords:
  - electronic health records
  - generative modelling
  - longitudinal trajectories
  - survival analysis
  - representation learning
  - UK Biobank
  - MIMIC-IV
